{
  "_about": [
    "Rules for the text cleanup after Whisper (M1 plan step 1). Shared by every app; the Rust reader is",
    "desktop/core/src/normalize.rs and the shared test cases are cases.json next to this file.",
    "Order: remove + replace characters, count scripts (needs_llm_ratio), romanize Urdu / Devanagari runs",
    "(whole word from *_words first, else letter by letter), drop phantoms, apply the user's word list, tidy spacing.",
    "Urdu letters that depend on their place (kept in code): waw at the start of a word = w; yeh at the start or",
    "before alef / waw = y; heh at the end after a consonant = a. Devanagari: consonants carry an 'a' that is",
    "dropped at the end of a word and between a vowel and a consonant with a vowel (schwa deletion).",
    "Phantoms: output that matches the last sentence(s) of the Whisper hint (spec/prompts/whisper-hint-v1.txt:",
    "the last one, the last two, ... the whole hint; Whisper echoes the hint's tail on silence) or a phantom",
    "phrase, within 1 word in 4, or that is only filler words, becomes empty text (D-007).",
    "Word list (D-014): exact match fixes the spelling; a fuzzy match needs the same sound skeleton and at least",
    "fuzzy_min_consonants consonants, so short everyday words are never changed."
  ],
  "remove": ["​", "‌", "‍", "‎", "‏", "؜", "ـ", "﻿"],
  "replace": {
